{id: "phy-ss1-1",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Kinetic Theory",examType: "WAEC",year: 2020,questionNumber: 1,question: "A few grains of table salt were put in a cup of cold water, kept at constant temperature and left undisturbed. Eventually all the water tasted salty. This action is due to?",options: {A: "convection",B: "osmosis",C: "capillarity",D: "diffusion"},correctOption: "D",explanation: "Diffusion is the movement of particles from a region of higher concentration to a region of lower concentration.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-2",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Circular Motion",examType: "WAEC",year: 2020,questionNumber: 2,question: "The force required to make an object of mass m, travelling with velocity v, turn in a circle of radius r is",options: {A: "mv²/r",B: "mr²/r",C: "mr/r",D: "mv/r²"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "Centripetal force F = mv²/r.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-3",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Momentum",examType: "WAEC",year: 2020,questionNumber: 3,question: "A machine gun with a mass of 5 kg fires a 50 g bullet at a speed of 100 m/s. The recoil speed of the machine gun is",options: {A: "0.5 m/s",B: "1.5 m/s",C: "1 m/s",D: "2 m/s"},correctOption: "C",explanation: "By conservation of momentum: 5 × V = 0.05 × 100 ⇒ V = 1 m/s.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-4",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Simple Pendulum",examType: "WAEC",year: 2020,questionNumber: 4,question: "If in a simple pendulum experiment the length of the inextensible string is increased by a factor of four, its period is increased by a factor of?",options: {A: "4",B: "π/2",C: "1/4",D: "2"},correctOption: "D",explanation: "T ∝ √L. If L becomes 4L, T becomes √4 = 2 times.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-5",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Thermal Expansion",examType: "WAEC",year: 2020,questionNumber: 5,question: "In what range of temperature is the expansion of water anomalous?",options: {A: "+208 °C to +212 °C",B: "−80 °C to −76 °C",C: "0 °C to +4 °C",D: "−4 °C to 0 °C"},correctOption: "C",explanation: "Water contracts from 0 °C to 4 °C instead of expanding.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-6",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Radioactivity",examType: "WAEC",year: 2020,questionNumber: 6,question: "Which of the following statements about radioactivity is true? (i) Alpha particle is positively charged (ii) Beta particle is negatively charged (iii) Gamma ray is neutral (iv) Beta particle has the same mass as helium atom (v) Gamma ray is charged.",options: {A: "i, ii, iii, iv only",B: "i, ii, iii only",C: "iv and v only",D: "i, ii and v only"},correctOption: "B",explanation: "Alpha is positive, beta is negative, gamma is neutral. Beta does not have the mass of helium; gamma is not charged.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-7",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Heat and Temperature",examType: "WAEC",year: 2020,questionNumber: 7,question: "In the study of Physics, temperature and heat are often confused with each other. Which of the following statements correctly defines these two elements?",options: {A: "Temperature is a measure of the average kinetic energy of the molecules of a substance",B: "Heat is a measure of the total kinetic energy of the molecules in a system",C: "Different materials require different amounts of heat to cause a given change in temperature",D: "All of the above"},correctOption: "D",explanation: "All three statements are correct definitions or facts about heat and temperature.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-8",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Current Electricity",examType: "WAEC",year: 2020,questionNumber: 8,question: "The effect of closing the key K in the circuit shown would be to?",options: {A: "increase the current by 0.4 A",B: "reduce the current by 0.4 A",C: "increase the current by 0.6 A",D: "reduce the current by 0.6 A"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "When K is open, R = 8 + 2 = 10 Ω. Closing K changes the total resistance and increases current by 0.4 A.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-9",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "X-rays",examType: "WAEC",year: 2020,questionNumber: 9,question: "Which of the following statements on the use of X-rays is incorrect? X-rays are used",options: {A: "in a hospital to obtain photographs of tissues and bones in the body",B: "for the treatment of malignant growths like cancer",C: "in detecting flaws in metallic castings",D: "in the sterilization of medical equipment"},correctOption: "D",explanation: "X-rays are not primarily used for sterilization of medical equipment; that is usually done by autoclaving or radiation like gamma rays.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-10",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Electromagnetic Waves",examType: "WAEC",year: 2019,questionNumber: 10,question: "Radio waves belong to the class of waves whose velocity is about",options: {A: "3 × 10⁸ m/s",B: "3 × 10⁶ m/s",C: "3 × 10¹⁰ m/s",D: "3 × 10⁵ m/s"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "All electromagnetic waves travel at the speed of light, approximately 3 × 10⁸ m/s in a vacuum.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-11",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Magnetism",examType: "WAEC",year: 2019,questionNumber: 11,question: "Which of the following statements about the electromagnet shown is correct?",options: {A: "A – B = S – N",B: "A – B = N – S",C: "The starting end of the current is south while the terminating end is north",D: "The magnetic field is uniform"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "Using the right-hand grip rule, the starting end becomes South and the terminating end North, so A–B = S–N.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-12",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Equilibrium",examType: "WAEC",year: 2019,questionNumber: 12,question: "A cone in unstable equilibrium has its potential energy",options: {A: "minimum",B: "maximum",C: "zero",D: "constant"},correctOption: "B",explanation: "In unstable equilibrium, the centre of gravity is at its highest point, so potential energy is maximum.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-13",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Free Fall",examType: "WAEC",year: 2019,questionNumber: 13,question: "Which of the following statements is/are correct for a freely falling body? I. The total energy is entirely kinetic II. The ratio of potential energy to kinetic energy is constant III. The sum of potential and kinetic energy is constant",options: {A: "I only",B: "II only",C: "III only",D: "I and II only"},correctOption: "C",explanation: "For a freely falling body, total mechanical energy (PE + KE) is conserved.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-14",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Conduction",examType: "WAEC",year: 2019,questionNumber: 14,question: "Efficiency of conduction in liquids and gases compared to solids is",options: {A: "more efficient",B: "less efficient",C: "the same",D: "not comparable"},correctOption: "B",explanation: "Solids conduct heat better than liquids and gases because their particles are closely packed.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-15",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Reflection",examType: "WAEC",year: 2018,questionNumber: 15,question: "An object is placed 20 cm from a concave mirror of focal length 10 cm. The linear magnification of the image produced is?",options: {A: "1",B: "2",C: "0.5",D: "3"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "Using 1/f = 1/v + 1/u, v = 20 cm. Magnification m = v/u = 1.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-16",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Electrical Circuits",examType: "WAEC",year: 2018,questionNumber: 16,question: "In homes, electrical appliances and lamps are connected in parallel because",options: {A: "it makes the appliances draw less current",B: "each appliance can be switched on or off independently",C: "it reduces the voltage across each appliance",D: "it increases the total resistance of the circuit"},correctOption: "B",explanation: "Parallel connection allows each appliance to operate independently with the same voltage.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-17",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Heat Transfer",examType: "WAEC",year: 2018,questionNumber: 17,question: "A room is heated by means of a charcoal fire; an occupant of the room standing away from the fire is warmed mainly by",options: {A: "conduction",B: "convection",C: "radiation",D: "reflection"},correctOption: "C",explanation: "Heat from the fire reaches the person mainly by radiation (infrared).",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-18",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Radioactivity",examType: "WAEC",year: 2018,questionNumber: 18,question: "Natural radioactivity consists of the emission of",options: {A: "alpha particles only",B: "beta particles only",C: "gamma rays only",D: "alpha particles, beta particles and gamma rays"},correctOption: "D",explanation: "Natural radioactivity involves emission of alpha, beta, and gamma radiation.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-19",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Change of State",examType: "WAEC",year: 2018,questionNumber: 19,question: "The process whereby a liquid turns spontaneously into vapour is called",options: {A: "boiling",B: "evaporation",C: "sublimation",D: "condensation"},correctOption: "B",explanation: "Evaporation is the spontaneous change of a liquid to vapour below its boiling point.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-20",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Specific Heat Capacity",examType: "WAEC",year: 2017,questionNumber: 20,question: "When two objects P and Q are supplied with the same quantity of heat, the temperature change in P is observed to be twice that of Q. The mass of P is half that of Q. The ratio of the specific heat capacity of P to Q is",options: {A: "1:1",B: "2:1",C: "1:2",D: "4:1"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "H = mcθ. Since H and relationships give mPcPθP = mQcQθQ, solving gives cP : cQ = 1:1.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-21",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Waves",examType: "WAEC",year: 2017,questionNumber: 21,question: "Which of the following is not a mechanical wave?",options: {A: "Sound wave",B: "Water wave",C: "Radio wave",D: "Wave in a closed pipe"},correctOption: "C",explanation: "Radio waves are electromagnetic waves and do not require a medium.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-22",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Optics",examType: "WAEC",year: 2017,questionNumber: 22,question: "Calculate the height of the image formed by a pinhole camera of length 12 cm used to photograph an object 60 cm away from the hole and 70 cm high.",options: {A: "14 cm",B: "28 cm",C: "7 cm",D: "35 cm"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "Magnification = 12/60 = 0.2. Image height = 0.2 × 70 = 14 cm.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-23",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Upthrust",examType: "WAEC",year: 2017,questionNumber: 23,question: "Calculate the upthrust on an object of volume 50 cm³ which is immersed in a liquid of density 10³ kg/m³ [g = 10 m/s²]",options: {A: "5.0 N",B: "2.5 N",C: "0.5 N",D: "0.05 N"},correctOption: "C",explanation: "Upthrust = ρVg = 1000 × 50×10⁻⁶ × 10 = 0.5 N.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-24",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Resonance",examType: "WAEC",year: 2017,questionNumber: 24,question: "Why do soldiers march disorderly while crossing a bridge?",options: {A: "To prevent resonance",B: "To increase the load on the bridge",C: "To reduce friction",D: "To increase their speed"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "Orderly marching can cause resonance, leading to bridge collapse.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-25",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Machines",examType: "WAEC",year: 2017,questionNumber: 25,question: "A block and tackle pulley arrangement has 6 pulleys in which an effort of 50 N supports a load of 200 N. Calculate the efficiency of the machine.",options: {A: "66.7%",B: "75%",C: "80%",D: "50%"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "Efficiency = (Load/Effort) × (1/VR) × 100%. VR = 6, so efficiency = (200/50)/6 × 100% = 66.7%.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-26",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Moments",examType: "WAEC",year: 2016,questionNumber: 26,question: "A metre rule is pivoted at its mid-point with a vertical force of 10 N hanging from a distance 30 cm from the mid-point. At what distance must a 15 N force hang to balance the ruler horizontally?",options: {A: "20 cm",B: "30 cm",C: "15 cm",D: "10 cm"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "10 × 30 = 15 × x ⇒ x = 20 cm.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-27",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Newton's Laws",examType: "WAEC",year: 2016,questionNumber: 27,question: "What force has to be exerted on a mass 60 kg to give it an acceleration of 10 m/s² vertically upwards? [g = 10 m/s²]",options: {A: "600 N",B: "1200 N",C: "300 N",D: "900 N"},correctOption: "B",explanation: "F = ma + mg = 60×10 + 60×10 = 1200 N.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-28",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Pinhole Camera",examType: "WAEC",year: 2016,questionNumber: 28,question: "If the distance between the object and the pinhole of a pinhole camera is reduced by half, the size of the image of the object",options: {A: "is quadrupled",B: "is halved",C: "remains the same",D: "is doubled"},correctOption: "D",explanation: "Image size is inversely proportional to object distance; halving distance doubles image size.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-29",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Atomic Physics",examType: "WAEC",year: 2016,questionNumber: 29,question: "An electron in a hydrogen atom makes a transition from the ground level to the third level. If the energy at the ground level is E₀, calculate the energy at the third level. [h = 6.6 × 10⁻³⁴ Js; f = 10¹⁵ Hz]",options: {A: "E₀/9",B: "E₀/3",C: "3E₀",D: "9E₀"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "Energy levels in hydrogen are proportional to 1/n², so E₃ = E₀/9.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-30",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Projectiles",examType: "WAEC",year: 2016,questionNumber: 30,question: "A projectile is fired from the ground level with a velocity of 300 m/s at an angle of 30° to the horizontal. Calculate the time taken to reach the maximum height. [g = 10 m/s²]",options: {A: "15 s",B: "30 s",C: "10 s",D: "20 s"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "T = u sinθ / g = 300 × sin30° / 10 = 15 s.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-31",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Cooling",examType: "WAEC",year: 2016,questionNumber: 31,question: "The rate of cooling of a heated quantity of liquid in an enclosure depends on the",options: {A: "nature of the surface",B: "colour of the container",C: "temperature difference",D: "all of the above"},correctOption: "D",explanation: "Rate of cooling depends on surface nature, colour, and temperature difference.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-32",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Energy",examType: "WAEC",year: 2021,questionNumber: 32,question: "A ball of mass 0.1 kg is thrown vertically upwards with a speed of 10 m/s from the top of a tower 10 m high. Neglecting air resistance, its total energy just before hitting the ground is? [g = 10 m/s²]",options: {A: "5 J",B: "10 J",C: "15 J",D: "20 J"},correctOption: "C",explanation: "Total energy = KE + PE = ½mv² + mgh = ½(0.1)(100) + (0.1)(10)(10) = 5 + 10 = 15 J.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-33",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Power",examType: "WAEC",year: 2021,questionNumber: 33,question: "A car of mass 800 kg attains a speed of 25 m/s in 20 s. The power developed in the engine is?",options: {A: "1.25 × 10⁴ W",B: "2.50 × 10⁴ W",C: "1.25 × 10⁶ W",D: "2.50 × 10⁶ W"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "Work done = ½mv² = ½(800)(625) = 250,000 J. Power = 250,000/20 = 12,500 W = 1.25 × 10⁴ W.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-34",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Friction",examType: "WAEC",year: 2021,questionNumber: 34,question: "When the brakes in a car are applied, the frictional force on the tyres is?",options: {A: "a disadvantage because it is in the direction of motion",B: "a disadvantage because it is in the opposite direction of motion",C: "an advantage because it is in the direction of motion",D: "an advantage because it is in the opposite direction of motion"},correctOption: "D",explanation: "Friction opposes motion, which is advantageous when braking.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-35",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Elasticity",examType: "WAEC",year: 2021,questionNumber: 35,question: "If the stress on a wire is 10⁷ N/m² and the wire is stretched from its original length of 10.00 m to 10.05 m, the Young's modulus of the wire is?",options: {A: "5.0 × 10⁻⁴ N/m²",B: "5.0 × 10⁻⁵ N/m²",C: "2.0 × 10⁻⁸ N/m²",D: "2.0 × 10⁹ N/m²"},correctOption: "D",explanation: "Strain = 0.05/10 = 0.005. Y = stress/strain = 10⁷ / 0.005 = 2.0 × 10⁹ N/m².",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-36",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Density",examType: "WAEC",year: 2021,questionNumber: 36,question: "A solid weighs 10.00 N in air, 6 N when forcefully immersed in water, and 7.0 N when fully immersed in a liquid X. Calculate the relative density of the liquid X.",options: {A: "5/3",B: "4/3",C: "3/4",D: "7/10"},correctOption: "C",explanation: "Upthrust in water = 4 N; upthrust in X = 3 N. Relative density = 3/4.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-37",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Pressure",examType: "WAEC",year: 2020,questionNumber: 37,question: "Two divers G and H are at depths 20 m and 40 m, respectively below the water surface in a lake. The pressure on G is P₁ while the pressure on H is P₂. If the atmospheric pressure is equivalent to 10 m of water, then the value of P₂/P₁ is?",options: {A: "2",B: "3",C: "5/3",D: "3/5"},correctOption: "C",explanation: "P₁ = 10 + 20 = 30 m water; P₂ = 10 + 40 = 50 m water. Ratio = 50/30 = 5/3.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-38",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Sound",examType: "WAEC",year: 2020,questionNumber: 38,question: "A ship travelling towards a cliff receives the echo of its whistle after 3.5 seconds. If the speed of sound in air is 250 m/s, how much closer is the ship to the cliff?",options: {A: "437.5 m",B: "875 m",C: "125 m",D: "250 m"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "Distance = speed × time/2 = 250 × 3.5 / 2 = 437.5 m.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-39",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Forces",examType: "WAEC",year: 2020,questionNumber: 39,question: "Consider three forces acting at O and in equilibrium. Which of the following equations is/are correct? I. P₁ cos θ₁ = P₂ cos θ₂ II. P₁ sin θ₁ = P₂ sin θ₂ III. P₁ = P₂ = P₃",options: {A: "I only",B: "II only",C: "I and II only",D: "I, II and III"},correctOption: "C",explanation: "For equilibrium, horizontal and vertical components must balance: P₁ cos θ₁ = P₂ cos θ₂ and P₁ sin θ₁ = P₂ sin θ₂.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-40",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Friction",examType: "WAEC",year: 2019,questionNumber: 40,question: "A boy pushes a 500 kg box along a floor with a force of 2000 N. If the velocity of the box is uniform, the coefficient of friction between the box and the floor is",options: {A: "0.8",B: "0.65",C: "0.4",D: "0.2"},correctOption: "C",explanation: "For uniform velocity, applied force = frictional force. μ = F/mg = 2000/(500×10) = 0.4.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-41",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Pressure",examType: "WAEC",year: 2019,questionNumber: 41,question: "A rectangular solid block has length 10 cm, breadth 5 cm and height 2 cm. If it lies on a horizontal surface, and has density 100 kg/m³, calculate the pressure it exerts on the surface.",options: {A: "20 Pa",B: "50 Pa",C: "100 Pa",D: "200 Pa"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "Mass = ρV = 100 × (10×5×2×10⁻⁶) = 0.01 kg. Weight = 0.1 N. Area = 10×5 cm² = 50×10⁻⁴ m². Pressure = 0.1 / (50×10⁻⁴) = 20 Pa.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-42",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Equilibrium",examType: "WAEC",year: 2019,questionNumber: 42,question: "A body was slightly displaced from its equilibrium position. Which one of the following is a condition for its stable equilibrium?",options: {A: "an increase in the kinetic energy of the body",B: "a decrease in the potential energy of the body",C: "an increase in the potential energy of the body",D: "no change in potential energy"},correctOption: "C",explanation: "In stable equilibrium, potential energy increases when displaced.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
{id: "phy-ss1-43",subjectId: "physics",grade: "SS1",term: "1st Term",topic: "Sound",examType: "WAEC",year: 2018,questionNumber: 43,question: "A man hears his echo from a nearby hill 2 s after he shouted. If the frequency of his voice is 260 Hz and the wavelength is 1.29 m, how far away is the hill?",options: {A: "335.4 m",B: "167.7 m",C: "670.8 m",D: "3354 m"},correctOption: "A",explanation: "Speed = fλ = 260 × 1.29 = 335.4 m/s. Distance = speed × time/2 = 335.4 × 2 / 2 = 335.4 m.",difficulty: "medium",verificationStatus: "AI_GENERATED_PRACTICE",contentType: "text"},
